# netsurf (MacSurf bridge): innerText puts a flex or grid container's items on their own lines
# Generated 2026-09-30
#
# Google's footer links read "PrivacyTerms AdvertisingBusinessAbout": they
# are flex items, which CSS blockifies -- each is a block-level box, so
# innerText gives each its own line ("Privacy\nTerms" in Chromium, also
# for grid and inline-flex containers). patch 168's rendered-text walk
# took the item's own display (inline <a>) and ran them together.
# vita_polyfill.js renderedText(): the walk carries the parent's display;
# an element child of a flex/grid/inline-flex/inline-grid container is
# treated as a block.
# Test: JS-innertext.html case 9 (9/9; Chromium gives the same string).
# Scorecard: google text 0.526 -> 0.658 (score 57.0 -> 62.9); the words
# still missing are the r3 reference's trending topics (live data).
